<title>USA: Cali buys two N.J. offices for $10.2 mln.</title>
<headline>Cali buys two N.J. offices for $10.2 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CRANFORD N.J. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cali Realty Corp said Thursday it has acquired the two class-A office properties in the Moorestown Corporate Center, Moorestown, N.J., for $10.2 million.</p>
<p>The properties, said Cali, were purchased from Metropolitan Life Insurance Co and financed through one of Cali's credit facilities.</p>
<p>Cali is a fully integrated, self-administered, self-managed real estate investment trust which owns 129 properties in New Jersey, New York, Pennsylvania and Connecticut.</p>
